WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.901
Every application that changes
passes four gates: its disposition,

2
00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:08.712
a design review, every pull
request, and every release.

3
00:00:08.712 --> 00:00:12.863
Two are meetings and two are
automation, and that's deliberate.

4
00:00:12.863 --> 00:00:16.964
The daily ones run in the pipeline,
on protected branches that bind

5
00:00:16.964 --> 00:00:21.288
administrators too, because a gate
that's run as a meeting gets skipped.

6
00:00:21.288 --> 00:00:25.419
Each gate leaves proof, so the evidence
builds up as the work happens,

7
00:00:25.419 --> 00:00:28.813
instead of screenshots the
month before an assessment.

8
00:00:28.813 --> 00:00:32.400
One threshold belongs to the
authorizing official alone:

9
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.437
when a change is significant enough
to reopen the authorization.

10
00:00:36.437 --> 00:00:39.376
Set it early, and let
design review apply it.

11
00:00:39.376 --> 00:00:40.750
Now, how it runs.
